From acacdb61346664afd4a84163d81587592d8debcd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 22:35:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Blu-ray: say why Java (BD-J) menus cannot run, and what to do

With the Java add-on of the LibreELEC repository installed ("JRE for BD-J menus",
tools.jre.zulu), Kodi still said that the Java runtime was missing (issue #1, 2026-10-24).
libbluray answers with two bits (BLURAY_DISC_INFO::libjvm_detected, bdj_handled), and Kodi
showed one text for both (#29804, which speaks of Java) and logged the reason with debugging
only. What stood in the way there was not Java: libbluray takes only the jar of its own version
(libbluray-j2se-1.5.1.jar for this build), the image has none, and the add-on brings that of
1.4.0, built in May. Another way to the same text is an add-on installed after Kodi started:
its profile (JAVA_HOME, and its lib folder with the X11 libraries that the JVM's AWT needs in
LD_LIBRARY_PATH) is read by kodi.sh when Kodi starts.

KODI::BLURAYJAVA (xbmc/filesystem/BlurayJava.h) tells five states from those bits, the
environment and whether the add-on is installed: ready, no runtime, a restart needed, a runtime
that does not load (with its JAVA_HOME), and the jar of this libbluray missing. The state goes
to kodi.log without debugging, when the disc setting is turned to the menu and when a disc with
BD-J titles opens; the dialog of the setting says what to do instead of #29804, and a disc whose
first title is a Java menu that cannot run says why in a notification, where the longest title
used to start without a word. The lines of libbluray's bdj.c that reach Kodi's logger (the
critical ones, a few per disc) go to the log without debugging too.

Nothing that plays changes. Tested on the host: the decision against stand-ins of the
environment (bdj_state_test.cpp; four mutations make it fail), and the syntax of the four files
with the compile commands of the last build. Strings in English, translated in Estuary (es_es,
es_ar, es_mx).
